#
# The failure the frontier layer exists to prevent, stated in full: a roster CUT BY A
# BUDGET, presented as closed, and carrying a witness that says so in so many words.
#
# The witness is not empty and not missing. It names the predicate it settled, states
# the budget it consumed, and is cited by the frontier — so the presence law
# (logic:FrontierCarriesSaturationWitnessConstraint) passes and the content legs of the
# closure law pass too. Its logic:resultEvaluation is logic:BudgetExhausted: the search
# stopped because it hit its declared bound, not because it reached a fixed point.
#
# What it costs in the world: the search was truncated at 64 units, the entry it had
# not yet reached was the rollback nobody could see, and the operator reads a roster
# certified complete. Every downstream reader of a closed frontier is entitled to treat
# absence as evidence of absence, which is exactly what makes an uncertified closure
# claim worse than no claim at all.
#
# It is the cut-budget case. The absence sibling
# (frontier-closed-without-saturation-witness.ttl) cites no witness and can only reach
# the presence law; the content-free sibling
# (frontier-cites-a-content-free-witness.ttl) cites a witness with no status to be
# exhausted. This one is the case where the evidence is present, readable, and says
# the opposite of what the frontier claims.
#
# MUST trip logic:FrontierClosureRequiresSaturationConstraint.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

ex:frontierCutForBudget a logic:ActionableFrontier ;
    rdfs:label "a roster claiming closure over a search its own witness says was cut"@en ;
    logic:frontierSaturationWitness ex:truncatedSaturation .

ex:truncatedSaturation a logic:SaturationWitness ;
    rdfs:label "a saturation witness recording the bound the search stopped at"@en ;
    logic:settledPredicate logic:hasFrontierEntry ;
    logic:consumedBudget "64"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    logic:resultEvaluation logic:BudgetExhausted .
